## Solution

**The process:** Start with input $a_0 = 7$. At each step $n$, compute $a_n = s(a_{n-1}^2) + 1$, where $s(x)$ is the digit sum of $x$.

**Tracing the sequence:**

| Step $n$ | Input $a_{n-1}$ | Square | Digit sum | $+1$ = $a_n$ |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 7 | 49 | 13 | **14** |
| 2 | 14 | 196 | 16 | **17** |
| 3 | 17 | 289 | 19 | **20** |
| 4 | 20 | 400 | 4 | **5** |
| 5 | 5 | 25 | 7 | **8** |
| 6 | 8 | 64 | 10 | **11** |
| 7 | 11 | 121 | 4 | **5** |

At step 7 we return to **5**, which was the value at step 4. Since the transformation is deterministic (a function of the current value alone), the sequence from step 4 onward enters a cycle:

$$5 \to 8 \to 11 \to 5 \to 8 \to 11 \to \cdots$$

This is a cycle of **period 3**, beginning at $a_4 = 5$.

**Finding $a_{1999}$:**

For all $n \ge 4$, the value is determined by the position within the cycle:

$$a_n = \begin{cases} 5 & \text{if } (n-4) \bmod 3 = 0 \\ 8 & \text{if } (n-4) \bmod 3 = 1 \\ 11 & \text{if } (n-4) \bmod 3 = 2 \end{cases}$$

Compute the index:

$$(1999 - 4) \bmod 3 = 1995 \bmod 3$$

Since $1995 = 3 \times 665$, we have $1995 \bmod 3 = 0$.

Therefore $a_{1999} = 5$.

**The system outputs $\boxed{5}$ at the conclusion of the 1999th step.**

